---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Figure1 = `console.log("Hello, world!");`;
const Figure2 = `Hello, world!`;
const Task1 = `console.log("Hello, world!");
`;
const Task2 = `console.log("Hello, world!");
console.log("My name is Jordan.");
console.log("This is my first program.");
`;
const Task3 = `console.log("Hello, world!");
console.log("My name is Jordan.");
console.log("This is my first program.");
console.log("");
console.log("Three true things about me:");
console.log("1. I have never written code before.");
console.log("2. I am taking this class because it fit my schedule.");
console.log("3. I once ate an entire pizza by myself.");
`;
const ExampleOutput = `Hello, world!
My name is Jordan.
This is my first program.

Three true things about me:
1. I have never written code before.
2. I am taking this class because it fit my schedule.
3. I once ate an entire pizza by myself.
`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 1.1: Welcome to AP CSP</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 1.1</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Welcome to AP CSP</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>What This Course Is</p>
              <p>How You Are Assessed</p>
              <p>Your First Program</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>You Do Not Need Any Experience</h2>
              <p>
                This course starts from zero. If you have never written a line
                of code, you are exactly where you are supposed to be.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>You Do Not Need Any Experience</h2>
              <p>
                If you <i>have</i> written code before, good &mdash; you will get
                to the interesting parts faster. But nothing this year assumes it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>What Is Computer Science Principles?</h2>
              <p>
                It is not only about writing code. It is about how computing
                works, what it can do, and what it does to people.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>The Five Big Ideas</h2>
              <ul>
                <li class="fragment"><b>Creative Development</b> &mdash; how programs get built</li>
                <li class="fragment"><b>Data</b> &mdash; how information is stored and used</li>
                <li class="fragment">
                  <b class="text-sn-theme">Algorithms and Programming</b> &mdash; the biggest slice
                </li>
                <li class="fragment"><b>Computer Systems and Networks</b> &mdash; how machines talk</li>
                <li class="fragment">
                  <b class="text-sn-theme">Impact of Computing</b> &mdash; who it helps and who it hurts
                </li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>How You Are Assessed</h2>
              <p>Two things, and they are very different.</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>How You Are Assessed</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>The Exam &mdash; 70%</dt>
                  <dd>
                    70 multiple-choice questions in 120 minutes, in May.
                  </dd>
                  <dt>The Create Task &mdash; 30%</dt>
                  <dd>
                    A program you design and build yourself, during class time.
                  </dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>The Create Task</h2>
              <p>
                You will hear about this all year, so it is worth knowing now
                what it actually is.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>The Create Task</h2>
              <p>
                You build a program of your own choosing. It must take{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">input</b>, store data in a{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">list</b>, use a{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">procedure you wrote yourself</b>, and
                produce <b class="text-sn-theme">output</b>.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">
                You get at least <b>nine hours of class time</b> to do it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>The Create Task</h2>
              <p>
                Every one of those four requirements is something we cover this
                quarter. By the time you start it, none of it will be new.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>What Is a Program?</h2>
              <p>
                A list of instructions, carried out in order, one at a time,
                exactly as written.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">
                That last part &mdash; <i>exactly as written</i> &mdash; is
                where most of your frustration this year will come from.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Your First Instruction</h2>
              <p>
                <CodeSnippet
                  code="console.log()"
                  lang={"javascript"}
                  theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                  inline
                /> displays a message as text.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Your First Instruction</h2>
              <Code
                code={Figure1}
                frame="code"
                title="Demo"
                lang="javascript"
                showLineNumbers={false}
                class="mb-3"
              />
              <Code
                code={Figure2}
                frame="terminal"
                lang="txt"
                title="Demo"
                showLineNumbers={false}
                class="fragment"
              />
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Reading That Line</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <ul>
                  <li class="fragment">
                    The <b>quotes</b> mark where your text starts and ends.
                  </li>
                  <li class="fragment">
                    The <b>parentheses</b> hold what you want displayed.
                  </li>
                  <li class="fragment">
                    The <b>semicolon</b> ends the instruction.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Describing what this course assesses</li>
                <li>Explaining what the Create task requires</li>
                <li>Writing and running a first program</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Program</dt>
                  <dd>
                    A list of instructions carried out in order, one at a time.
                  </dd>
                  <dt>Statement</dt>
                  <dd>A single instruction in a program.</dd>
                  <dt>Output</dt>
                  <dd>Information a program produces.</dd>
                  <dt>Create Performance Task</dt>
                  <dd>
                    A program you build during class that counts for 30% of your
                    AP score.
                  </dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Create a new <b>JavaScript</b> program named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">1-1-hello</b>.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: One Line</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Write the single line below exactly as shown.</li>
            <li>Run your program.</li>
            <li>
              If nothing happens, or you see red text, check your quotes,
              parentheses, and semicolon before asking for help. Then ask.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <Code
            code={Task1}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Welcome to AP CSP"
          />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: Introduce Yourself</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Add two more lines so the program says who you are.</li>
            <li>Run your program after <i>every</i> line you add.</li>
            <li>
              <b class="text-sn-theme">Note</b>: the green lines with a + sign
              are new code. Don't type the + sign.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <Code
            code={Task2}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Welcome to AP CSP"
            ins={{ range: "2-3" }}
          />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 3: Three True Things</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Add a blank line of output, a heading, and three numbered facts
              about yourself. Keep them school appropriate.
            </li>
            <li>
              A <CodeSnippet
                code='console.log("");'
                lang={"javascript"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> with nothing between the quotes prints an empty line.
            </li>
            <li>Yours should say different things than the example.</li>
          </ul>

          <Code
            code={Task3}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Welcome to AP CSP"
            ins={{ range: "4-8" }}
          />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Challenge (Optional): Break It on Purpose</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Make a copy of one working line, then remove one thing from the
              copy &mdash; a quote, a parenthesis, or the semicolon.
            </li>
            <li>Run it and read the error message.</li>
            <li>
              Write down what the error said. You will see these all year, and
              they are more helpful than they look.
            </li>
            <li>Put the line back the way it was before submitting.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Verify your program works correctly.</p>

          <Code
            code={ExampleOutput}
            frame="terminal"
            lang="txt"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            title="Example Output"
            mark={{
              label: "Your facts should be different",
              range: "6-8",
            }}
          />
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer the following questions before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>
              The Create task requires input, a list, a procedure you wrote, and
              output. Without knowing what any of those mean yet, which one
              sounds hardest to you, and why?
            </li>
            <li>
              A program does exactly what you write, not what you meant. Describe
              a time something else in your life worked that way.
            </li>
            <li>
              What is one thing you want to be able to build by the end of this
              year?
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit the required files to the appropriate dropbox.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
